## Returns ok("ok") when float difference is within `epsilon`, otherwise err(`msg`).
## @deprecated Use `check_eq_float_native` instead.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `a`: the actual value.
## - `b`: the expected value.
## - `msg`: the error payload used when the values differ. Borrowed.
## - `epsilon`: the inclusive tolerance. Defaults to `0.000001`.
##
## ## Retorno
## The legacy `oracle.ResultString` (owned by the caller): `ok("ok")` when
## `|a - b| <= epsilon`, `err(msg)` otherwise.
##
## ## Memoria
## The returned `ResultString` owns its string field; release it with `banish`.
## The parameters are borrowed.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## let r as ResultString is calling ward.check_eq_float with 1.0, 1.0, "not equal"
## ```
weave check_eq_float with a as float , b as float , msg as string , epsilon as float is 0.000001 into ResultString:
    let diff as float is if (a - b) < 0.0 then (b - a) else (a - b)
    if diff <= epsilon:
        return calling oracle.result_ok_string with "ok"
    return calling oracle.result_err_string with msg

